  "content": "CLARIFY:\n1. Are the VMs running on esxi-pay-05 identical in configuration and application tier to those running on esxi-pay-07 and esxi-pay-08? because if esxi-pay-05 carries a different mix of workloads (e.g., more batch or cache-heavy apps), the high NVMe read bandwidth and active memory are expected for its specific role and not a cluster-wide anomaly.\n2. Was sql-pay-03 on esxi-pay-05 before the weekend, or was it migrated or powered on after Tuesday 09:00? because if it arrived via DRS after the weekend, its 256 GB of non-tiered memory instantly reduced the DRAM available for tiered VMs, forcing them to NVMe and explaining the spike in reads and latency.",
